WEBVTT

00:45.045 --> 00:47.965
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:48.257 --> 00:52.344
EPISODE 8

00:52.427 --> 00:54.555
Yeah, dig there. Right there.

00:54.638 --> 00:56.265
That, that rock there...

00:58.475 --> 01:00.686
Okay, the wind and rain are getting worse.

01:00.769 --> 01:02.271
Everyone, evacuate
to the barracks for now.

01:02.354 --> 01:03.647
Fall back!

01:03.730 --> 01:05.816
- Fall back!
- Fall back!

01:05.899 --> 01:07.776
Hey, fall back!

01:07.859 --> 01:10.612
- Careful, careful!
- Everyone, move out carefully!

01:10.696 --> 01:11.905
Look after all your comrades, got it?

01:11.989 --> 01:14.283
- Hurry, hurry!
- Hurry, let's move!

01:14.741 --> 01:16.285
My glasses!

01:16.368 --> 01:17.619
My glasses, my glasses!

01:18.495 --> 01:19.663
GANGLIM

01:21.623 --> 01:22.958
Are you okay?

01:29.881 --> 01:31.341
Kang Seong-jae!

01:34.428 --> 01:35.554
GANGLIM OUTPOST

01:39.933 --> 01:41.602
GANGLIM

01:50.319 --> 01:52.404
- You okay?
- Are you all right, sir?

01:52.487 --> 01:55.032
It'll take more than this for me,
Hwang Seok-ho, to...

01:58.577 --> 01:59.828
I'm fine.

02:07.711 --> 02:09.046
Wait, wait, wait...

02:10.339 --> 02:11.423
I think my arm is broken.

02:11.506 --> 02:12.507
I think it's broken.

02:12.591 --> 02:14.718
No, if you think it's broken,
this won't do.

02:14.801 --> 02:15.802
You gotta pull it harder, see?

02:16.303 --> 02:17.721
- That's how a broken arm sets.
- I said

02:17.804 --> 02:20.098
I think it's broken. I think.

02:20.182 --> 02:22.100
- So it's not actually broken?
- Right.

02:22.184 --> 02:23.685
Jeez.

02:23.769 --> 02:25.228
Are you doing this on purpose?

02:25.312 --> 02:28.482
Why would I do this on purpose?
I've got no reason, Company Commander.

02:28.565 --> 02:31.318
The way you jumped in
to protect Kang Seong-jae...

02:31.401 --> 02:34.154
I really thought I was watching
a scene from a movie.

02:34.488 --> 02:35.572
I, Hwang Seok-ho...

02:36.156 --> 02:37.783
As long as I can protect the men

02:37.866 --> 02:39.910
I won't go down even with broken bones.

02:40.160 --> 02:41.912
Still, you were being reckless.

02:41.995 --> 02:44.122
What if it had hit you in the head?

02:44.206 --> 02:46.500
I'd just need to wear a cast
and I'd be fine...

02:46.583 --> 02:48.960
But if one soldier gets in an accident,
it becomes a huge headache.

02:49.044 --> 02:50.295
Goodness.

02:50.379 --> 02:51.963
That's our Company Commander for you.

02:52.047 --> 02:53.215
No matter what happens

02:53.298 --> 02:55.092
never take your eye off the prize.

02:55.175 --> 02:56.301
My "prize"?

02:56.385 --> 02:57.386
What's that supposed to mean?

02:57.469 --> 02:59.971
Hey, why are you getting so serious
over a little joke?

03:00.222 --> 03:02.891
I mean, to our Company Commander,
promotion is everything.

03:02.974 --> 03:05.352
So the safety of the soldiers
is your meal ticket, isn't it?

03:05.435 --> 03:08.146
Shouldn't you be more concerned,
Master Sergeant?

03:08.230 --> 03:09.606
Your juniors have made Sergeant Major.

03:09.690 --> 03:11.066
Will you retire as a Master Sergeant?

03:12.192 --> 03:14.611
I should pull this harder. Really hard.

03:14.695 --> 03:16.446
What's wrong with you two?

03:16.738 --> 03:18.532
- Stop it.
- It hurts.

03:18.615 --> 03:20.367
Company Commander, we have a huge problem.

03:21.576 --> 03:24.663
The rain is so heavy that
it washed out Ganglim Bridge.

03:26.164 --> 03:27.249
Wait a minute.

03:27.958 --> 03:28.959
If the Ganglim Bridge is blocked...

03:29.793 --> 03:31.962
we can't get out of the outpost.

03:32.379 --> 03:33.547
That's right.

03:33.630 --> 03:34.631
Goodness...

03:35.340 --> 03:36.758
we're in real trouble now.

03:46.977 --> 03:48.854
What's with all this chaos
all of a sudden?

03:48.937 --> 03:51.273
I've never seen it
rain this hard in my life.

03:51.356 --> 03:53.942
This is due to the abnormal climate
caused by global warming, sir.

03:54.025 --> 03:56.570
Have you considered
you're the weird one for worrying?

03:56.737 --> 03:57.738
I'm sorry?

03:57.821 --> 03:59.948
Oh, wait! Isn't that the chicken coop?

04:02.367 --> 04:03.368
The chicken coop?

04:04.119 --> 04:05.662
Wait! They're not supposed to fly.

04:15.338 --> 04:19.426
GANGLIM OUTPOST
ISOLATION DAY 1

04:19.509 --> 04:24.347
GANGLIM

04:37.486 --> 04:40.405
THOROUGH VIGILANCE AND FLAWLESS MISSIONS

04:52.375 --> 04:53.960
What... How...

04:55.128 --> 04:56.963
- Damn...
- What... What do we do?

04:57.214 --> 04:59.257
- I don't know, just get inside.
- Yes, sir.

05:08.683 --> 05:10.018
Are these all the ingredients
we have left?

05:10.101 --> 05:12.813
The storage shed flooded,
so there's not much that's usable.

05:12.979 --> 05:14.981
Today was delivery day

05:15.315 --> 05:17.567
so we'd used up most of what we had.

05:19.444 --> 05:20.570
If the Ganglim Bridge is cut off

05:20.654 --> 05:22.030
that means we can't get any ration.

05:25.325 --> 05:27.494
It looks like today's going to be tough.

05:30.455 --> 05:32.791
We'll be resupplied soon,
so let's just hang in there.

05:35.460 --> 05:36.503
Why don't I have service?

05:37.546 --> 05:38.547
What's wrong with it?

05:39.673 --> 05:40.674
Salute.

05:40.924 --> 05:42.968
The distribution box is completely shot.

05:43.051 --> 05:45.846
Since the power's out,
the communications relay is dead too.

05:45.929 --> 05:47.389
- And cell phones have no service.
- Company Commander.

05:47.722 --> 05:51.434
We moved ingredients from the fridge
into coolers for now...

05:51.768 --> 05:53.895
But I don't think they'll last very long.

05:58.400 --> 05:59.401
Master Sergeant.

05:59.484 --> 06:01.486
How many combat rations are left?

06:01.778 --> 06:04.072
We only have a three-day supply
of combat rations.

06:04.155 --> 06:05.407
The regulations only call
for three days' worth.

06:06.950 --> 06:07.951
Three days.

06:09.286 --> 06:10.954
We'll hold out for three days.

06:11.621 --> 06:12.622
Sir?

06:12.706 --> 06:16.042
The Battalion Commander won't give up
on Ganglim easily.

06:17.294 --> 06:20.422
Based on his infinite trust in me,
he'll be sure

06:20.589 --> 06:21.756
to handle this quickly.

06:21.965 --> 06:22.966
Without a doubt.

06:23.717 --> 06:24.718
MILITARY COMBAT RATIONS

06:24.801 --> 06:26.052
We just finished training

06:26.136 --> 06:27.762
and now we're back to combat rations?

06:27.971 --> 06:29.306
Corporal Joo Sang-uk...

06:29.389 --> 06:31.016
is it true we can't get any supplies?

06:31.099 --> 06:33.518
The Ganglim Bridge is out,
so we can't do anything right now.

06:34.185 --> 06:35.562
Damn it.

06:35.854 --> 06:37.856
What if things aren't fixed

06:37.939 --> 06:39.149
when we run out of combat rations?

06:39.482 --> 06:42.152
What do you think will happen?
We'll all just starve to death.

06:45.238 --> 06:46.615
I don't know either.

06:46.698 --> 06:47.699
I'm sure they'll fix it soon.

06:48.033 --> 06:49.492
I mean, it's not like they'll let us
starve to death, right?

06:53.622 --> 06:55.290
Class Change Quest Round 2.

06:55.373 --> 06:56.917
Typhoon on a Meal Tray.

06:57.167 --> 06:59.961
Find hidden cooking ingredients
and serve a meal.

07:00.045 --> 07:02.881
Maintain the Mess Hall
Satisfaction Rating above 50.

07:03.423 --> 07:04.424
Failure to do so

07:04.507 --> 07:07.135
- will terminate The Chef's Path.
- What...

07:08.136 --> 07:10.680
What am I supposed to do
with combat rations?

07:12.515 --> 07:15.185
Man, changing my class is so hard.

07:17.145 --> 07:18.939
GANGLIM

07:29.908 --> 07:31.076
Attention!

07:31.785 --> 07:34.371
No matter how fearsome nature may be...

07:34.663 --> 07:36.247
we will never be broken!

07:36.331 --> 07:37.582
Unbreakable spirit!

07:37.999 --> 07:42.170
We will show them the power of Ganglim!

07:51.972 --> 07:53.306
Carry on.

07:56.226 --> 07:57.978
With both his arms broken...

07:58.061 --> 07:59.562
what does he mean "unbreakable"?

07:59.646 --> 08:01.439
Still, I thought he was pretty cool.

08:11.116 --> 08:12.325
Hello, Do-yeon.

08:12.951 --> 08:14.494
- You're here.
- Yes, I'm here.

08:14.995 --> 08:16.621
- Se-chan.
- Yes, hello.

08:16.830 --> 08:19.708
I'm not your principal, so why are you
bowing at 90 degrees? I'm your wife.

08:19.958 --> 08:21.751
- Please, relax.
- Oh, relax.

08:21.960 --> 08:24.295
- Relax, relax. Treat me like a friend.
- Okay, I will.

08:25.380 --> 08:26.715
What's wrong with me?

08:32.012 --> 08:33.388
GANGLIM OUTPOST
ISOLATION DAY 2

08:44.315 --> 08:46.026
The rain stopped...

08:46.901 --> 08:49.571
but why do I feel so drained?

08:49.654 --> 08:52.323
If you ask me, it's these combat rations.

08:57.996 --> 08:59.706
Hey, how much longer do we
have to eat this stuff?

08:59.789 --> 09:01.082
I'm already sick of it.

09:01.166 --> 09:04.377
I'm starting to miss the shit soup
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun used to make.

09:04.461 --> 09:06.546
Pick something worth missing.

09:06.629 --> 09:07.922
Even so...

09:08.006 --> 09:09.466
the combat rations are better.

09:09.549 --> 09:10.800
Isn't that obvious?

09:10.884 --> 09:12.469
These are combat rations

09:13.011 --> 09:16.473
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol boiled himself.

09:29.569 --> 09:31.321
If we keep serving combat rations

09:31.738 --> 09:33.281
aren't the guys
going to burn down the mess hall?

09:34.991 --> 09:37.786
Mess Hall Satisfaction Rating
is decreasing.

09:37.994 --> 09:39.204
Please be cautious.

09:46.503 --> 09:48.129
Isn't there some way

09:48.713 --> 09:51.132
to make these combat rations taste better?

09:52.133 --> 09:53.885
Seafood paella.

09:54.094 --> 09:56.179
A traditional Spanish home-cooked meal.

09:56.304 --> 09:57.388
What?

09:58.681 --> 10:01.184
How am I supposed to make paella
in a situation like this?

10:02.268 --> 10:05.146
Find the hidden ingredients
to complete the paella.

10:05.230 --> 10:08.024
OBJECTIVE: THREE SEAFOOD ITEMS, TWO SPICES

10:08.566 --> 10:09.567
Seafood?

10:25.458 --> 10:28.044
First seafood ingredient acquired.

10:28.128 --> 10:30.004
BIG AND FRESH WHELKS

10:46.146 --> 10:47.438
KOREAN FROZEN SHRIMP

10:47.939 --> 10:50.942
Second seafood ingredient acquired.

10:57.657 --> 10:59.159
What are you so happy about?

10:59.492 --> 11:00.618
Well...

11:02.078 --> 11:03.163
It's nothing.

11:03.246 --> 11:04.581
Well, Corporal Kim.

11:05.123 --> 11:08.042
I'm going to need some seafood.

11:08.126 --> 11:11.129
What are you talking about?
Where would you find seafood around here?

11:14.716 --> 11:15.717
Wait.

11:17.051 --> 11:19.596
Master Sergeant's... squid?

11:25.768 --> 11:27.020
Jeez.

11:45.538 --> 11:46.581
Wait...

11:47.290 --> 11:48.416
Where did he get that?

11:48.499 --> 11:51.419
I gave one I found in the warehouse,
and he's been at it all day.

11:55.632 --> 11:57.383
What's everyone staring at?

11:57.675 --> 11:59.135
Get back to your duties.

11:59.219 --> 12:01.387
I told you I'll let you know.

12:01.471 --> 12:03.681
Don't you trust me, Hwang Seok-ho?

12:03.973 --> 12:06.935
We'll be out of combat rations
by tomorrow.

12:07.352 --> 12:08.645
Come on, Company Commander.

12:08.895 --> 12:11.022
I'll try to get the power back on
at the outpost

12:11.105 --> 12:12.523
so why don't you stop messing around

12:12.607 --> 12:14.108
and do something productive for a change?

12:14.192 --> 12:17.487
The Battalion Commander
is going to send support to Ganglim

12:17.695 --> 12:20.323
so let's just wait a bit.
All right? Don't worry.

12:20.406 --> 12:22.784
Are they gonna bring us supplies
from the Korean War?

12:23.826 --> 12:24.827
Get out.

12:25.620 --> 12:27.330
We're gonna starve at this rate.

12:27.538 --> 12:28.581
I said, get out.

12:31.334 --> 12:33.086
Fine, have it your way.
Do whatever you want.

12:33.169 --> 12:34.337
Good grief.

12:35.421 --> 12:37.131
I never should have given him that thing.

12:37.382 --> 12:38.841
- Jeez.
- Salute.

12:41.052 --> 12:42.053
Goodness.

12:47.267 --> 12:48.309
I've never faced

12:48.393 --> 12:50.186
a disaster like this before.

12:52.188 --> 12:53.189
No.

12:55.525 --> 12:58.152
I, Hwang Seok-ho, will get this done.

12:58.236 --> 13:02.240
Did you see the Company Commander's legs
shaking while saying everything's fine?

13:02.699 --> 13:04.242
I'm so scared out of my mind.

13:05.118 --> 13:06.160
Tell me about it.

13:07.328 --> 13:09.622
We'll all starve to death
waiting for a rescue.

13:10.790 --> 13:12.041
All because we're stuck
with a lousy commander.

13:12.458 --> 13:14.627
Salute. Private First Class Kang Seong-jae
reporting to the admin office.

13:14.711 --> 13:16.004
Yeah. What's up?

13:16.254 --> 13:17.297
Is something wrong at the mess hall?

13:17.672 --> 13:19.007
Master Sergeant.

13:19.590 --> 13:20.633
Can I have the squid, please?

13:21.551 --> 13:22.552
What?

13:23.720 --> 13:25.138
Well, will you look at this kid.

13:25.471 --> 13:27.598
What, did you get a whiff of it? Here.

13:28.891 --> 13:31.352
Not this, I need a lot more than this.

13:34.355 --> 13:35.440
What are you talking about?

13:43.197 --> 13:44.282
SQUID

13:44.991 --> 13:46.951
You know the domestic ones
are rare, right?

13:47.035 --> 13:48.036
Thank you.

13:48.745 --> 13:49.746
But...

13:51.039 --> 13:52.165
this one too.

13:53.833 --> 13:56.669
I don't know what kind of masterpiece
you're trying to make...

13:58.588 --> 14:01.257
You better not let
this squid's sacrifice be in vain.

14:01.424 --> 14:02.425
Got it?

14:03.176 --> 14:06.554
I'll make something delicious
that meets your expectations.

14:08.848 --> 14:09.932
Go on.

14:10.475 --> 14:11.476
Yes, sir.

14:11.809 --> 14:12.810
I said, go on.

14:19.442 --> 14:20.443
Salute!

14:25.573 --> 14:26.574
ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE

14:29.369 --> 14:32.246
All seafood ingredients acquired.

14:36.751 --> 14:39.504
SQUID, BIG AND FRESH WHELKS,
KOREAN FROZEN SHRIMPS

14:39.587 --> 14:43.466
3 SEAFOOD ITEMS: WHELKS, SHRIMP, SQUID
2 SPICE ITEMS

14:49.639 --> 14:54.811
SPICES ACQUIRED: 0 OF 2

15:00.108 --> 15:01.818
SPICES ACQUIRED: 0 OF 2

15:09.325 --> 15:12.495
First spice acquired.

15:13.496 --> 15:14.497
TASTY CURRY
MILDLY SPICY

15:14.580 --> 15:16.124
- I see.
- Hey, Kang Seong-jae.

15:16.833 --> 15:18.042
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

15:18.126 --> 15:19.710
What are you up to now?

15:22.338 --> 15:24.674
I'm trying to make paella
with the combat rations.

15:25.550 --> 15:27.760
- Pa... what?
- Well, it's...

15:27.844 --> 15:29.971
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol,
are we having combat rations again?

15:30.179 --> 15:31.305
You punk.

15:31.472 --> 15:35.143
When your senior cooks, you eat.
What's with all the complaining?

15:35.226 --> 15:38.438
We've been eating combat rations
since the last training.

15:39.188 --> 15:41.149
- Hey, Kang Seong-jae.
- Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

15:41.232 --> 15:44.402
Can't you make something delicious,
like those fried rice balls?

15:44.527 --> 15:45.528
Hey!

15:45.862 --> 15:47.155
He already said he's making

15:47.613 --> 15:49.407
some paella or whatever

15:49.490 --> 15:51.033
- so just shut up and wait.
- What?

15:54.454 --> 15:55.455
Paella?

15:56.247 --> 16:00.042
Isn't that the Spanish dish
that's easy to make but delicious?

16:00.418 --> 16:01.419
Oh, really?

16:03.129 --> 16:04.589
You squeeze a bunch of lemon

16:04.672 --> 16:07.383
on the seafood...

16:07.800 --> 16:09.969
It's like...

16:10.052 --> 16:12.138
one of those fancy foreign dishes.

16:12.680 --> 16:13.973
But no matter what, our rookie...

16:15.975 --> 16:17.810
- can't pull that off.
- Right.

16:19.729 --> 16:21.606
Lemon juice. Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

16:21.689 --> 16:23.274
That's right, I need lemon juice.

16:23.357 --> 16:26.110
Where are we gonna get lemon juice?
We don't even have lemons.

16:26.402 --> 16:29.071
Just wing it.
You're going to spoil the other guys.

16:29.780 --> 16:31.324
- Lemon...
- Hero.

16:31.616 --> 16:34.285
Use the "Comrade, help me" skill.

16:34.660 --> 16:36.204
COMRADE, HELP ME! LEVEL 1

16:38.456 --> 16:39.457
Wait.

16:44.378 --> 16:45.588
I know just the guy.

16:53.721 --> 16:55.181
Yes?

16:55.264 --> 16:56.307
Salute...

16:56.641 --> 16:58.935
Salute! Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol,
reporting on official business, sir.

16:59.018 --> 17:00.811
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.
What's this about?

17:00.895 --> 17:04.315
Could I have some of that lemon juice
you were drinking the other day?

17:04.398 --> 17:05.650
My lemon juice?
What are you talking about?

17:05.900 --> 17:08.444
That lemon juice's for my detox to enhance

17:08.528 --> 17:09.904
my combat abilities.

17:09.987 --> 17:11.447
It's not something
I can give away to anyone.

17:11.531 --> 17:13.533
You seem busy, so I'll help myself.

17:13.616 --> 17:15.284
Thank you. Salute!

17:15.368 --> 17:18.287
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol!
Kim Kwan-cheol! Kim Kwan-cheol!

17:18.371 --> 17:19.830
That's mine!

17:20.289 --> 17:21.290
Hey!

17:46.691 --> 17:47.984
WHEN THE BROTH REDUCES, ADD SEAFOOD
AND SIMMER THEN ADD LEMON JUICE

17:49.068 --> 17:50.611
HEALTHY LEMON JUICE

18:10.881 --> 18:12.133
It is time for the evening meal.

18:12.216 --> 18:13.843
Go ahead and have your meal.

18:19.390 --> 18:22.143
It is time for the evening meal.
Go ahead and have your meal.

18:24.478 --> 18:27.773
Man, I'm so hungry I could eat anything.

18:29.108 --> 18:30.568
Anything but combat rations.

18:31.485 --> 18:33.779
It's combat rations for dinner too, sir.

18:38.701 --> 18:41.245
Give me a break.

18:43.164 --> 18:44.582
You should at least eat a little.

18:50.379 --> 18:52.673
This army life really sucks.

19:18.532 --> 19:20.409
Olé!

19:20.660 --> 19:22.370
Olé!

19:22.662 --> 19:24.205
Olé!

19:35.508 --> 19:38.803
Perfect! This is delicious!

19:41.472 --> 19:43.766
Paella made from combat rations.

19:45.476 --> 19:47.103
Delicious.

19:47.645 --> 19:50.815
Perfect! This is delicious!

19:51.315 --> 19:54.944
- Perfect! This is delicious!
- Perfect! This is delicious!

19:59.824 --> 20:00.908
Thank you.

20:07.957 --> 20:10.793
Mess hall satisfaction is increasing.

20:11.085 --> 20:12.837
Oh, delicious!

20:28.811 --> 20:30.020
Charge!

20:32.148 --> 20:33.149
One, two, three!

20:40.614 --> 20:46.412
GANGLIM OUTPOST
ISOLATION DAY 3

20:47.830 --> 20:51.083
Do your worst, typhoon.

20:51.417 --> 20:53.627
We will be victorious!

20:53.961 --> 20:57.173
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

20:57.256 --> 20:58.257
Man...

20:58.883 --> 21:01.469
A meal from Kang Seong-jae
really gives you a boost, huh?

21:03.888 --> 21:07.141
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

21:25.284 --> 21:27.077
Finally, the power's back on.

21:31.540 --> 21:32.666
The fridge is working now, too.

21:34.043 --> 21:35.795
I bet the new supplies
will get here soon, right?

21:36.545 --> 21:38.255
We're running low on ingredients too, sir.

21:38.380 --> 21:39.423
Hey.

21:39.590 --> 21:42.092
Now, is the power working okay?

21:42.176 --> 21:43.928
Yes, the fridge's working properly.

21:44.011 --> 21:46.305
Yeah, that's what I like to see.

21:46.931 --> 21:47.932
Hey, Kwan-cheol.

21:49.058 --> 21:50.351
You helping your junior out?

21:50.434 --> 21:53.479
- Yes, sir.
- Keep up the good work, all right?

21:53.646 --> 21:54.772
Work hard

21:54.855 --> 21:56.315
and I might even get you off
overnight guard duty.

21:56.398 --> 21:57.566
Come on, sir, don't mess with me.

21:57.733 --> 21:59.568
- I'm serious, man.
- Really?

22:00.903 --> 22:01.904
Just kidding.

22:02.530 --> 22:04.198
- Hey, Mr. Kang.
- Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

22:04.281 --> 22:05.324
Follow me.

22:15.292 --> 22:16.502
All right.

22:16.585 --> 22:17.795
- Hold on.
- Yes, sir.

22:25.803 --> 22:26.971
All right.

22:27.137 --> 22:28.138
And...

22:29.598 --> 22:31.016
last but not least...

22:31.350 --> 22:32.518
Here.

22:42.903 --> 22:43.904
Here.

22:44.864 --> 22:46.198
LIKEABILITY

22:46.282 --> 22:47.700
LIKEABILITY 100%

22:51.078 --> 22:52.830
New colleague has been added.

22:53.080 --> 22:54.832
Master Sergeant Park Jae-young.

22:59.003 --> 23:01.672
Aren't these your most prized possessions?

23:01.881 --> 23:03.424
In an emergency like this

23:03.674 --> 23:05.718
you squeeze blood from a stone, right?

23:05.926 --> 23:07.970
I figured you'd need these more than I do.

23:09.930 --> 23:11.974
Isn't the supply truck coming soon?

23:12.057 --> 23:14.435
We're out of combat rations after today.

23:15.102 --> 23:17.313
Comms are back up

23:17.688 --> 23:19.356
so the truck should be here soon.

23:19.440 --> 23:21.567
YEONJU-SI TYPHOON RELIEF SUPPLIES
BONGGIL TRADING

23:26.363 --> 23:27.364
Salute!

23:28.407 --> 23:30.200
Is the damage assessment
for each unit complete?

23:30.451 --> 23:32.286
The recovery is being delayed.
What's the status on Ganglim?

23:32.494 --> 23:33.621
Still no contact?

23:33.746 --> 23:35.122
There's a problem with the Ganglim Bridge

23:35.205 --> 23:36.624
but don't worry too much, sir.

23:36.707 --> 23:39.960
Every unit keeps a week's worth of
combat rations for situations.

23:40.044 --> 23:41.462
It's probably nothing...

23:41.545 --> 23:43.505
but maybe because Seok-ho is there...

23:43.756 --> 23:45.007
I have this uneasy feeling.

23:46.050 --> 23:48.010
I understand how you feel,
Battalion Commander.

23:48.093 --> 23:51.055
There's not a single sane person
stationed at Ganglim.

23:51.680 --> 23:52.681
Hello.

23:53.223 --> 23:55.225
- Salute.
- You're here.

23:55.643 --> 23:56.894
Well, now, look who it is.

23:57.019 --> 23:58.312
If it isn't our esteemed governor.

23:58.979 --> 24:00.648
- We appreciate all your hard work.
- Of course, sir.

24:00.940 --> 24:03.067
Did you make it home okay
after our game of golf the other day?

24:03.567 --> 24:05.486
- That day, I...
- OK, taking the picture now.

24:06.862 --> 24:08.697
One, two!

24:08.781 --> 24:10.449
Wait, hold on.

24:10.532 --> 24:11.992
4TH COMPANY COMMANDER, HWANG SEOK-HO

24:12.368 --> 24:14.328
Oh, my apologies.

24:14.703 --> 24:17.122
RESPECTED BATTALION COMMANDER

24:17.206 --> 24:19.166
Battalion Commander! Battalion...

24:19.917 --> 24:20.918
What...

24:22.002 --> 24:23.003
Why isn't he...

24:25.589 --> 24:26.799
RESPECTED BATTALION COMMANDER

24:29.468 --> 24:30.678
RESPECTED BATTALION COMMANDER

24:32.513 --> 24:34.515
Sir! 4th Company Commander,
Hwang Seok-ho, reporting.

24:34.598 --> 24:36.183
- Battalion Commander, sir...
- Is everything all right?

24:36.392 --> 24:37.935
I heard from the Support Section Chief.

24:38.018 --> 24:40.646
That each outpost has a week's
supply of combat rations.

24:41.647 --> 24:42.856
Well, Battalion Commander.

24:42.940 --> 24:45.693
There's been a misunderstanding.

24:45.985 --> 24:46.986
What are you talking about?

24:47.403 --> 24:48.487
Well, you see...

24:50.280 --> 24:53.575
The only combat rations we had
were a three-day supply.

24:53.659 --> 24:55.285
And we've already used up most of that.

24:55.369 --> 24:58.706
Why are you just reporting this to me now?

25:00.416 --> 25:01.583
- I'm sorry?
- I told the Regimental Commander

25:01.667 --> 25:03.252
that everything was fine at Ganglim.

25:03.335 --> 25:06.380
Now how am I supposed to tell him
we're out of combat rations?

25:06.672 --> 25:08.549
- I...
- Jeez.

25:09.091 --> 25:10.092
Just hang in there.

25:10.342 --> 25:11.343
But how are we supposed to...

25:11.427 --> 25:13.095
That's why you need to file
your reports properly!

25:14.138 --> 25:15.139
RESPECTED BATTALION COMMANDER

25:16.432 --> 25:17.433
Battalion Commander.

25:17.516 --> 25:18.726
Battalion Commander!

25:18.809 --> 25:20.102
We're starving!

25:27.234 --> 25:28.694
How cute.

25:30.529 --> 25:32.322
Gosh, I'm so bored.

25:40.414 --> 25:42.416
Now what in the world does that mean, huh?

25:42.499 --> 25:45.294
- What's the big idea?
- Come on, this is ridiculous!

25:45.377 --> 25:47.963
All the support went to civilian aid.
What can I do?

25:48.547 --> 25:51.175
So let's just monitor
the situation for a bit.

25:51.258 --> 25:54.011
Goodness, that Lee Min-gu... That jerk!

25:54.094 --> 25:56.930
Civilian aid, my foot.
We're about to starve to death.

25:57.014 --> 25:58.766
I'm gonna go up that mountain

25:58.849 --> 26:00.350
and forage for some greens myself.

26:00.434 --> 26:03.270
- Just letting you all know.
- Hey, don't be ridiculous.

26:03.353 --> 26:05.981
So, what? You want us to sit back
and starve to death?

26:06.982 --> 26:08.567
- Jeez, seriously!
- Master Sergeant!

26:10.319 --> 26:11.987
GANGLIM OUTPOST
ISOLATION DAY 4

26:17.993 --> 26:19.369
What's on the menu today?

26:19.453 --> 26:20.621
We're out of combat rations.

26:20.704 --> 26:22.247
All that's left is the ramen, sir.

26:22.539 --> 26:23.916
Then is there any kimchi?

26:23.999 --> 26:25.709
We're out of kimchi as well, sir.

26:26.043 --> 26:28.462
Just shut up and eat.
Now's not the time to be picky.

26:28.545 --> 26:29.546
Come here.

26:30.714 --> 26:32.132
Why's he always yelling at me...

26:33.801 --> 26:35.052
Thanks for the food.

26:44.019 --> 26:45.729
There was barely any food,
so there's nothing to clean up.

26:46.021 --> 26:47.940
Hey, but what are we gonna eat now?

26:48.023 --> 26:49.274
We finished all the ramen, didn't we?

26:52.277 --> 26:53.403
Yes, sir.

26:53.487 --> 26:55.197
Well, we're screwed now.

26:56.698 --> 26:57.950
Damn it...

26:58.158 --> 26:59.535
Does anyone have a secret stash?

27:00.327 --> 27:01.370
Hero.

27:10.879 --> 27:13.590
Well... there is one thing
that comes to mind.

27:17.094 --> 27:18.387
Actually, it's probably a bad idea.

27:18.637 --> 27:19.638
Why?

27:20.639 --> 27:22.099
What is it? Spit it out!

27:31.191 --> 27:32.860
BARRACKS 1
YOON DONG-HYUN

27:33.277 --> 27:34.403
If Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun finds out

27:34.486 --> 27:35.988
we'll be in trouble, won't we?

27:36.071 --> 27:37.156
Oh, come on.

27:37.364 --> 27:40.075
We're about to starve.
Is this really the time to be scared?

27:40.284 --> 27:41.994
Don't we need to get our hands on

27:42.077 --> 27:43.495
anything we can eat?

27:44.955 --> 27:46.290
Right, exactly.

27:46.665 --> 27:48.125
We need to look out for ourselves first.

27:53.922 --> 27:55.674
There's nothing here, damn it.

28:04.766 --> 28:05.851
CHICKEN BREAST BEST SET

28:06.810 --> 28:07.811
Ah, screw it!

28:19.239 --> 28:20.949
There!

28:23.327 --> 28:24.620
Let's eat!

28:28.081 --> 28:29.958
We're saved. We're saved!

28:30.042 --> 28:31.835
BLACK PEPPER CHICKEN BREAST

28:32.920 --> 28:35.672
You have acquired a cooking ingredient.

28:54.233 --> 28:55.609
CHICKEN PORRIDGE: ADD SALT, PEPPER,
AND FINISH OFF WITH SESAME OIL

28:55.692 --> 28:57.402
SEASON WITH PEPPER

29:15.295 --> 29:16.755
Decent chicken porridge.

29:16.838 --> 29:20.008
DECENT CHICKEN PORRIDGE
COULD'VE BEEN SOMEONE'S SOURCE OF PROTEIN

29:31.186 --> 29:34.147
GANGLIM OUTPOST
ISOLATION DAY 5

29:43.865 --> 29:44.866
Is this for real?

29:45.158 --> 29:47.411
We've gone through all our supplies.

29:47.494 --> 29:48.495
All that's left is rice.

29:48.578 --> 29:49.579
I'm sorry.

29:56.920 --> 29:58.046
Hey, Pyo Ji-yong.

29:58.338 --> 29:59.381
You got anything in your barracks?

29:59.464 --> 30:00.757
What would I have?

30:00.841 --> 30:02.592
Come on, don't be like that.
Just give me some.

30:03.010 --> 30:04.303
Hey, what are comrades for?

30:04.386 --> 30:06.346
We're supposed to share,
especially when times are tough.

30:07.264 --> 30:08.265
Freeze.

30:08.348 --> 30:10.559
What was that? That sound from your
military biscuit pocket?

30:12.769 --> 30:14.563
Hey, what are you doing?

30:14.730 --> 30:16.648
The hunger must be making you hear things.

30:17.733 --> 30:21.987
No, that was the unmistakable crinkle
of a snack bag.

30:27.492 --> 30:29.453
I swear, I have nothing. Nothing.

30:29.536 --> 30:31.496
Why are you doing this? Really!

30:31.580 --> 30:34.750
- I swear, I have nothing!
- I heard it! Right here! Look.

30:37.961 --> 30:39.087
This is my last one.

30:41.631 --> 30:43.425
Just one bite. Just one bite.

30:44.051 --> 30:45.469
Just one bite, please. Come on.

30:47.846 --> 30:49.765
- I can't! No!
- Please!

30:49.848 --> 30:51.725
No way.

31:02.569 --> 31:04.279
CHOCO PIE

31:09.368 --> 31:11.453
CHOCO PIE

31:21.004 --> 31:22.089
No!

31:40.774 --> 31:41.775
Freeze!

31:43.110 --> 31:44.694
What do you all think you're doing?

32:00.961 --> 32:03.505
Company Commander, this is a serious
problem on our hands.

32:03.964 --> 32:06.425
You should speak with the
Battalion Commander and recommend

32:06.508 --> 32:08.176
we evacuate the outpost.

32:08.260 --> 32:10.512
And just how are we supposed to
evacuate the outpost?

32:10.595 --> 32:12.848
The Ganglim Bridge is out.
We can't get in or out.

32:13.265 --> 32:14.349
Right.

32:15.350 --> 32:18.186
Then I'll go out
and find something. All right?

32:18.270 --> 32:21.314
If I bring something back,
won't Seong-jae figure something out?

32:22.149 --> 32:24.276
Didn't I tell you no?

32:24.359 --> 32:26.736
It's too dangerous! The rain just stopped.

32:26.820 --> 32:29.448
But we can't just sit here
and starve to death.

32:29.531 --> 32:32.284
- We have nothing to eat right now.
- Then I'll go with you.

32:32.367 --> 32:34.244
We can't just stand by and do nothing.

32:34.327 --> 32:35.745
No. I'll go with him.

32:35.829 --> 32:37.330
With the Company Commander's condition

32:37.456 --> 32:38.874
you have to stay and protect the outpost.

32:39.124 --> 32:40.250
That's enough, everyone.

32:41.126 --> 32:42.669
Absolutely not. I said no.

32:42.752 --> 32:44.296
I, Hwang Seok-ho,
will absolutely not allow it.

32:44.379 --> 32:46.465
I'll contact the
Battalion Commander again...

32:46.548 --> 32:49.843
How long are we supposed to sit and wait?

32:49.926 --> 32:51.803
They care about themselves, not us.

32:51.887 --> 32:53.638
Company Commander, you frustrate me.

32:53.722 --> 32:54.848
That's how we get...

32:56.641 --> 32:58.185
stabbed in the back.

33:00.270 --> 33:01.771
What did you just say?

33:01.855 --> 33:03.315
Stabbed in the back? Frustrating?

33:03.398 --> 33:05.233
- Master Sergeant.
- What, was I wrong?

33:05.317 --> 33:06.485
We got stabbed in the back.

33:06.568 --> 33:08.236
All of us got stabbed
in the back, didn't we?

33:08.320 --> 33:09.571
Regardless of anything else...

33:10.572 --> 33:13.241
we can't let the soldiers starve.

33:21.750 --> 33:23.251
Fine. Do as you please.

33:24.169 --> 33:25.629
But if anything goes wrong...

33:26.296 --> 33:27.380
I, Hwang Seok-ho

33:28.173 --> 33:29.925
will hold you personally responsible.

33:44.064 --> 33:45.524
Don't go too far

33:45.607 --> 33:47.776
and make sure you're back before sunset.

33:48.360 --> 33:49.402
All right.

33:50.612 --> 33:52.072
- Pull this down.
- Yes, sir.

33:52.739 --> 33:54.574
Now, now, Outpost Commander.
Don't you worry.

33:54.658 --> 33:55.867
Who do you think I am?

33:55.951 --> 33:57.994
I'm Park Jae-young,
Master Sergeant of Ganglim Outpost.

33:58.078 --> 34:00.413
I can't let our soldiers starve to death.

34:00.497 --> 34:02.040
Deputy Outpost Commander, don't get hurt.

34:02.123 --> 34:03.416
Yes, ma'am. Don't worry.

34:04.334 --> 34:07.170
By the way, is the Company Commander
doing any better?

34:13.468 --> 34:15.345
Master Sergeant! Deputy Outpost Commander!

34:15.679 --> 34:16.888
You have to come back safely.

34:17.222 --> 34:18.682
Master Sergeant.

34:18.765 --> 34:20.308
Troops, attention!

34:20.934 --> 34:22.644
Salute the Master Sergeant!

34:22.727 --> 34:24.604
- Salute!
- Salute!

34:26.690 --> 34:28.108
Salute!

34:39.035 --> 34:40.078
I'll be back.

34:44.416 --> 34:45.417
Kang Seong-jae!

34:46.001 --> 34:47.002
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae!

34:47.085 --> 34:48.461
Get a fire going in the cauldron.

34:48.962 --> 34:51.631
- I'll be back before you know it.
- We love you, Master Sergeant!

34:55.302 --> 34:59.264
Over the desolate mountains and rivers

34:59.347 --> 35:01.933
- Let's go.
- The snow-covered

35:02.017 --> 35:08.440
Front line we march on...

35:22.370 --> 35:23.371
Oh, man.

35:23.955 --> 35:26.082
Okay, grab on.

35:33.214 --> 35:34.215
Jeez.

35:41.348 --> 35:42.766
Well, this is strange.

35:43.558 --> 35:44.559
What's wrong?

35:44.809 --> 35:46.645
I'm sure this was the right path.

35:47.354 --> 35:49.314
Maybe it's because the typhoon
swept through here?

35:49.814 --> 35:51.274
It all looks the same.

35:51.566 --> 35:52.567
Hey.

35:52.734 --> 35:55.487
Haven't we been climbing
that tree for a while now?

35:56.571 --> 35:57.989
I think we have.

35:58.198 --> 36:00.200
Jeez, it's like we're being haunted
by a ghost.

36:00.492 --> 36:03.161
We just keep going around in circles.

36:04.579 --> 36:06.915
A... a ghost, you say?

36:09.668 --> 36:10.669
Did I ever tell you...

36:11.211 --> 36:13.797
how the previous Master Sergeant died?

36:15.965 --> 36:16.966
No, you haven't.

36:18.259 --> 36:19.427
Well, the thing is...

36:20.387 --> 36:22.263
He was on patrol one night...

36:23.098 --> 36:24.808
and it was probably somewhere around here.

36:25.308 --> 36:26.810
Someone from behind kept...

36:28.645 --> 36:29.646
Never mind. It's nothing.

36:29.729 --> 36:32.065
Master Sergeant, we should head down
before it gets any later.

36:32.148 --> 36:33.775
The Company Commander is probably
waiting for us too.

36:33.858 --> 36:34.859
I'm kidding! Kidding, kidding.

36:34.943 --> 36:36.486
The last Master Sergeant is alive.

36:36.569 --> 36:38.988
Why would you joke like that?

36:40.198 --> 36:42.283
The soldiers are starving.
This is no time for games.

36:42.742 --> 36:43.743
Let's see.

36:44.119 --> 36:45.537
Okay, look.

36:45.620 --> 36:48.915
The sun is over there,
so we have to head that way.

36:48.998 --> 36:50.625
Are you sure it's that way,
Master Sergeant?

36:52.585 --> 36:54.003
My gut tells me so.

36:54.212 --> 36:56.297
I think your gut is the reason we're lost.

36:56.381 --> 36:57.382
Let's go.

36:57.757 --> 36:58.758
Wait up!

36:59.884 --> 37:02.762
We haven't eaten much,
so we have no energy.

37:03.430 --> 37:06.224
Hey, talking a lot makes you hungrier.

37:06.307 --> 37:07.308
Just be quiet.

37:07.392 --> 37:08.435
Master Sergeant.

37:09.310 --> 37:11.563
When on earth are you coming back?

37:11.646 --> 37:18.653
VIGILANCE IS OUR MISSION
GANGLIM OUTPOST

37:24.284 --> 37:25.368
What are you guys doing?

37:26.745 --> 37:27.787
If we do this...

37:28.413 --> 37:31.458
won't someone from above
see us and rescue us?

37:35.879 --> 37:37.172
YEONJU-SI TYPHOON RELIEF SUPPLIES
BONGGIL TRADING

37:38.757 --> 37:42.177
You must've been swamped leading
so many men for civilian support.

37:43.136 --> 37:44.888
Thanks to you, Battalion Commander

37:44.971 --> 37:47.849
I'll be able to hold my head high.

37:48.850 --> 37:52.270
Isn't it a soldier's duty to be
the first to step up?

37:53.271 --> 37:55.106
If I can be of help to you,
Regimental Commander

37:55.190 --> 37:56.399
I should take the lead on anything.

37:58.318 --> 37:59.694
On the next promotion list...

38:00.570 --> 38:01.988
your name will be on it,
Battalion Commander.

38:04.032 --> 38:05.033
Really?

38:06.451 --> 38:08.036
I know you've been anxious about it...

38:08.703 --> 38:09.871
so I'm giving you a heads-up.

38:13.833 --> 38:17.212
You had a tough time last year
because of Major Im.

38:17.754 --> 38:19.631
And I was worried

38:19.714 --> 38:21.007
things would be difficult for you.

38:21.549 --> 38:23.510
But seeing you break through
it all like this...

38:24.260 --> 38:25.386
I'm so relieved.

38:26.179 --> 38:28.181
Better days are coming.
Let's just hang in there.

38:30.225 --> 38:31.226
Take care, sir.

38:31.559 --> 38:32.560
Salute!

39:14.143 --> 39:15.311
Are they gonna be okay?

39:15.687 --> 39:19.232
I think we need the Master Sergeant here
as soon as possible.

39:28.283 --> 39:30.869
This is exactly why
I was against this! See?

39:30.952 --> 39:32.871
What now?

39:32.954 --> 39:33.955
I mean...

39:34.581 --> 39:38.084
What if they get stranded
in the middle of the night?

39:38.167 --> 39:39.836
Then I'll go out and find them, sir.

39:39.919 --> 39:41.671
You want to get stranded too, Cho Ye-rin?

39:45.466 --> 39:48.469
- Sir, you can't take that off now.
- I, Hwang Seok-ho

39:49.137 --> 39:50.722
value the safety of the outpost soldiers

39:50.805 --> 39:52.515
over my own two arms.

39:54.475 --> 39:55.518
But, sir...

39:56.269 --> 39:59.397
I'll go find them myself. In my place

39:59.480 --> 40:01.107
I need you to take command of the unit.

40:04.152 --> 40:05.361
Master Sergeant!

40:21.336 --> 40:22.337
Attention!

40:22.503 --> 40:23.671
Salute the Company Commander!

40:24.047 --> 40:25.340
- Salute!
- Salute!

40:29.302 --> 40:31.220
He's not returning the salute.
As you were.

40:31.596 --> 40:33.306
Master Sergeant Park Jae-young

40:33.389 --> 40:35.141
has completed our mission.

40:35.391 --> 40:39.437
We gathered balloon flower roots,
mushrooms, and mountain greens.

40:39.520 --> 40:40.521
Now we just need to get this
to Seong-jae...

40:40.605 --> 40:42.857
What in the world happened?
You weren't answering!

40:44.484 --> 40:45.485
What?

40:46.569 --> 40:49.322
Weren't you the one who said,
"Do as you please"?

40:50.031 --> 40:51.157
Don't tell me you were worried about us.

40:51.240 --> 40:52.408
It's not that I was worried.

40:52.492 --> 40:56.079
I distinctly remember telling you
it was dangerous after the rain.

40:56.329 --> 40:58.081
The Master Sergeant was incredible, sir.

40:58.164 --> 41:00.208
He was zipping around the
mountainside like a flying squirrel

41:00.291 --> 41:01.292
then suddenly back here again.

41:01.376 --> 41:03.127
What would you have done
if something had happened?

41:04.045 --> 41:05.505
Do as you please.

41:06.047 --> 41:07.840
You're an absolute mess.

41:09.509 --> 41:11.427
There he goes again,
bitching about something.

41:11.511 --> 41:13.012
He bitches when I leave.

41:13.096 --> 41:14.514
He bitches when I come back safely.

41:14.597 --> 41:16.557
If I were him, I'd have made Major
instead of wasting time bitching.

41:17.225 --> 41:19.227
The Company Commander may talk like that

41:19.310 --> 41:21.729
but he was really worried about you two.

41:22.313 --> 41:24.607
But the Company Commander
took off his cast.

41:26.067 --> 41:27.068
Yeah.

41:28.611 --> 41:29.862
I guess it's all healed.

41:30.905 --> 41:32.573
He's the type to do whatever
he wants, right?

41:32.699 --> 41:33.908
Probably just took it off
when he felt like it.

41:33.992 --> 41:37.829
- "Do as you please!"
- Welcome back! Great work!

41:47.171 --> 41:48.381
Heave-ho.

41:50.717 --> 41:51.926
CHAMNAMUL
GRADE A

41:52.010 --> 41:53.011
SHEPHERD'S PURSE, BALLOON FLOWER
GRADE A

41:53.094 --> 41:54.095
SHIITAKE MUSHROOM
GRADE A

41:54.178 --> 41:55.388
OYSTER MUSHROOM, COASTAL HOG FENNEL
GRADE A

41:55.471 --> 41:56.556
- Wow.
- What is all this?

41:57.724 --> 41:58.933
Did they raid the entire mountain?

41:59.017 --> 42:01.477
This is incredible.
How did they get all of this?

42:18.578 --> 42:19.579
MOUNTAIN GREENS BIBIMBAP

42:28.713 --> 42:29.797
PROFICIENCY
NAMUL COOKING LEVEL 7

42:29.881 --> 42:32.133
Your namul cooking proficiency
is increasing.

42:37.096 --> 42:38.806
- I think you can take them out now.
- Right.

42:46.522 --> 42:49.067
SAUTE SHIITAKE AND OYSTER MUSHROOMS
IN PERILLA OIL

43:12.799 --> 43:16.010
FRESH MOUNTAIN GREENS BIBIMBAP

43:16.094 --> 43:18.012
Fresh mountain greens bibimbap.

43:18.096 --> 43:20.556
CAPTURING THE VIBRANT
COLORS OF NATURE

43:23.726 --> 43:25.728
Company Commander, it's time to eat.

43:28.356 --> 43:31.651
The Master Sergeant said an injured person
needs to eat well to recover.

43:34.987 --> 43:37.698
I think that's why he pushed himself
so hard to go to the mountain.

43:56.592 --> 43:58.594
- Great work.
- Goodness.

43:59.595 --> 44:02.181
- Enjoy your meal.
- This smells amazing.

44:02.265 --> 44:03.266
Wow, this looks so good.

44:03.349 --> 44:04.725
You all worked hard.

44:05.309 --> 44:07.270
- Now, enjoy the food.
- Yes, sir.

44:07.645 --> 44:09.188
- I'm not hurt.
- Master Sergeant.

44:09.272 --> 44:12.066
- Yeah, eat up, eat up.
- Enjoy your meal.

44:12.150 --> 44:14.193
- Thank you for the meal.
- Yes, enjoy.

44:15.194 --> 44:17.822
Man, you must still be full.

44:19.532 --> 44:20.908
Are you waiting for the Company Commander?

44:20.992 --> 44:22.326
Oh, me?

44:22.618 --> 44:25.913
Why on earth would I wait
for the Company Commander?

44:25.997 --> 44:28.541
- Come on, let's just eat.
- Salute!

44:29.417 --> 44:30.418
At ease.

44:30.877 --> 44:32.044
Company Commander.

44:32.253 --> 44:33.296
Please come this way.

44:43.598 --> 44:44.599
Here you are.

44:46.350 --> 44:49.187
I was wondering
what all the fuss was about...

44:50.771 --> 44:52.440
but it looks pretty good.

45:00.489 --> 45:03.075
All right, everyone, let's eat up.

45:03.576 --> 45:05.620
- Enjoy your meal.
- Enjoy your meal.

45:06.746 --> 45:08.706
Go on, mix it all up and have a taste.

45:08.956 --> 45:12.084
Since you're such a picky eater,
I have no idea if you'll like it.

45:14.378 --> 45:17.089
Oh, come on. Stop it.

45:17.798 --> 45:19.467
- If you don't like it, don't eat it.
- No, that's not...

45:39.070 --> 45:40.947
All that hard work for nothing.

45:41.030 --> 45:42.531
And yet he's sure wolfing down
that bibimbap.

45:45.284 --> 45:46.702
This is good.

45:46.827 --> 45:47.828
Look at you.

45:47.912 --> 45:50.581
You're licking the spoon
clean and pretending you don't like it.

45:53.167 --> 45:55.544
- No, I just said it was good.
- You're pretending.

45:55.628 --> 45:58.172
I was just trying to say that...

46:03.094 --> 46:04.595
Thank you for the meal, Master Sergeant.

46:05.096 --> 46:06.472
Enjoy your meal, Company Commander.

46:18.526 --> 46:19.694
I, Hwang Seok-ho...

46:20.319 --> 46:21.862
have something I'd like to say
to all of you.

46:23.948 --> 46:25.199
Like this bibimbap

46:25.283 --> 46:26.492
I never doubted

46:26.575 --> 46:28.619
that our Ganglim would become one.

46:30.121 --> 46:32.331
What doesn't kill you makes you stronger,
as they say.

46:33.499 --> 46:35.751
The rain may have trapped us
and made us suffer

46:36.043 --> 46:39.255
but today, with this bibimbap,
we will become even stronger.

46:42.800 --> 46:43.926
I, Hwang Seok-ho...

46:44.552 --> 46:45.594
propose a toast

46:46.637 --> 46:48.472
with this bibimbap.

46:50.433 --> 46:52.727
When I say "Ganglim!"

46:52.852 --> 46:55.146
you all say "Forever."

46:55.229 --> 46:57.148
Ready? Ganglim!

46:57.231 --> 46:59.775
- Forever!
- Forever!

47:09.452 --> 47:13.247
Hero. Mess Hall Satisfaction Rating
has increased.

47:13.331 --> 47:15.791
MESS HALL SATISFACTION RATING
CURRENT STATUS 100

47:16.625 --> 47:19.170
As ingredients with their characters
mix together

47:19.337 --> 47:22.298
to create one delicious bowl of
bibimbap...

47:24.842 --> 47:28.679
we grew dependable and passionate
when we were together.

47:45.363 --> 47:46.489
Man...

47:47.156 --> 47:48.574
I'm on leave...

47:49.241 --> 47:51.243
and time is still crawling by.

47:51.994 --> 47:55.373
It's weird, but I think
I was more comfortable back on base.

47:55.581 --> 47:57.124
Hey, you idiot!

47:58.334 --> 48:00.878
What is this crazy fool saying?

48:00.961 --> 48:03.381
There's so much fun to be had.

48:03.464 --> 48:04.548
Get a grip, Dong-hyun.

48:04.632 --> 48:05.633
Yeah, get a grip.

48:12.348 --> 48:13.682
Enjoy your meal.

48:25.444 --> 48:26.695
That's weird.

48:27.696 --> 48:30.241
The taste seems different than before.

48:32.284 --> 48:34.787
Is it because I'm just used to
Kang Seong-jae's cooking?

48:36.705 --> 48:38.040
No, no way. Ugh!

48:38.165 --> 48:40.793
The military has launched civilian support
operations in Gangwon-do

48:40.876 --> 48:42.962
which was hit by Typhoon Crow.

48:43.462 --> 48:47.007
Oh, boy. You're all working so hard,
aren't you?

48:47.091 --> 48:49.593
- Goodness.
- They will support the civilians.

48:49.927 --> 48:52.721
However, with major roads
and bridges washed out

48:52.805 --> 48:55.599
supply routes and access
to some areas and military units

48:55.683 --> 48:57.101
have been severely disrupted.

48:57.560 --> 48:58.978
According to an official

48:59.061 --> 49:00.938
the government and military are mobilizing
all available personnel

49:01.021 --> 49:03.315
to accelerate recovery efforts

49:03.649 --> 49:06.318
but due to the widespread damage
caused by the typhoon

49:06.402 --> 49:08.988
they are facing significant difficulties
in resolving the situation.

49:09.071 --> 49:10.322
Up next...

49:16.287 --> 49:17.455
Master Sergeant.

49:17.788 --> 49:20.416
Do you have particular tastes in alcohol?

49:20.875 --> 49:23.669
Tastes? If it's expensive,
I'm just thankful.

49:23.752 --> 49:25.421
Whoa, it's blue.

49:25.838 --> 49:27.590
You got any snacks to go with this?

49:29.091 --> 49:30.634
I have something I really like.

49:31.635 --> 49:32.678
Star Candy.

49:33.846 --> 49:36.974
You think I want to be doing this?

49:38.601 --> 49:41.228
I'd love to stand up to my superiors too.

49:41.312 --> 49:42.313
But...

49:42.813 --> 49:44.398
as for me, Hwang Seok-ho...

49:45.774 --> 49:48.444
I graduated dead last
from the Military Academy.

49:49.612 --> 49:53.407
That's a well-known fact
for anyone in uniform.

49:54.867 --> 49:56.577
You're supposed to let it dissolve.

49:57.912 --> 50:01.165
Some of them come from
three generations of soldiers.

50:01.248 --> 50:04.502
And some are
ridiculously good at kissing up.

50:04.585 --> 50:06.337
- So what am I?
- Yeah.

50:06.420 --> 50:08.088
I mean, how bad must it be...

50:08.631 --> 50:11.884
for me to keep liquor
I don't even drink in my room?

50:11.967 --> 50:15.179
Hey, if you had such good stuff,
you should've brought it out earlier.

50:16.472 --> 50:18.224
Because you always drink makgeolli.

50:18.307 --> 50:20.142
Hey, you just don't get it.

50:20.351 --> 50:22.561
Once you acquire the taste,
nothing is better than makgeolli.

50:22.645 --> 50:24.897
See? This is why I didn't want
to give you any.

50:24.980 --> 50:26.148
"Do as you wish."

50:27.483 --> 50:29.401
- Do as you wish.
- Yes.

50:29.485 --> 50:31.111
- As you wish.
- Jeez.

50:33.113 --> 50:34.698
But why do you...

50:34.782 --> 50:38.285
always choose to do
the things you're told not to?

50:39.578 --> 50:42.081
With due respect, Company Commander

50:42.373 --> 50:44.542
aren't you the one who forbids everything?

50:47.461 --> 50:49.672
Someone said...

50:50.464 --> 50:52.800
that you have a surprisingly
fiery temper...

50:54.134 --> 50:56.762
and they were worried you'd get hurt
if left alone.

50:59.682 --> 51:00.683
Are you sincerely

51:01.267 --> 51:02.977
worried about me?

51:03.269 --> 51:06.355
Because I made a promise.

51:10.818 --> 51:14.071
I made a promise
to not let anyone get hurt.

51:16.740 --> 51:17.950
But it's not easy.

51:19.034 --> 51:20.578
It's all my fault.

51:21.745 --> 51:23.581
Me too. I'm just as much to blame.

51:25.291 --> 51:28.836
Since I don't have any power yet. Well...

51:30.045 --> 51:31.463
What can I do?

51:31.547 --> 51:32.798
Come on.

51:32.923 --> 51:35.759
Power's something you make,
isn't it, Company Commander?

51:36.510 --> 51:37.511
Look at what happened today.

51:37.595 --> 51:42.016
The camaraderie we couldn't build
finally came together.

51:43.601 --> 51:44.727
Come on.

51:44.810 --> 51:45.853
Have a drink.

52:08.125 --> 52:09.126
Yes?

52:15.674 --> 52:16.967
Salute.

52:17.217 --> 52:19.178
Oh, Seong-jae. What is it?

52:24.266 --> 52:25.643
During the last training exercise, ma'am.

52:27.353 --> 52:28.354
I happened to...

52:29.647 --> 52:33.859
overhear Captain Lee Min-gu on a call.

52:35.402 --> 52:36.737
A call? About what?

52:42.201 --> 52:43.202
He said...

52:43.827 --> 52:46.455
the Outpost Commander
won't be able to do anything now...

52:47.748 --> 52:49.291
and that if you became a nuisance...

52:49.375 --> 52:52.127
he would take care of it.

52:55.255 --> 52:56.340
What's that supposed to mean?

52:58.050 --> 53:01.303
I heard him mention your name,
Outpost Commander.

53:03.555 --> 53:05.808
Oh, you're talking about
Cho Ye-rin, right?

53:09.019 --> 53:10.020
Should I just take care of her?

53:14.400 --> 53:16.276
No, you must have heard wrong.

53:16.443 --> 53:18.696
Why would Captain Lee Min-gu
say something like that?

53:21.824 --> 53:23.033
Stop thinking about it

53:23.117 --> 53:24.368
and get some sleep.

53:28.163 --> 53:29.248
Yes, ma'am.

53:32.918 --> 53:34.002
Salute.

53:34.086 --> 53:36.588
OUTPOST COMMANDER'S OFFICE

54:15.669 --> 54:16.879
GANGLIM OUTPOST

54:26.305 --> 54:28.223
Did you see that?
The power of Hwang Seok-ho!

54:31.477 --> 54:33.228
- I am Hwang Seok-ho.
- Good work.

54:33.312 --> 54:34.980
- Hwang Seok-ho.
- All right, good work.

54:35.063 --> 54:36.815
Hey, you worked hard.

54:36.899 --> 54:39.276
But was it really possible
to restore the Ganglim Bridge so quickly?

54:39.359 --> 54:40.861
That's because...

54:41.862 --> 54:43.489
Yeah, yeah, knock it off. That's enough.

54:43.572 --> 54:45.032
- How's it looking, Seong-jae?
- Yes?

54:45.115 --> 54:46.825
We'll be able to eat properly now.

54:46.909 --> 54:49.411
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

54:52.331 --> 54:53.957
Salute! Are you all right, sir?

54:54.583 --> 54:55.584
Hey, Yoon Dong-hyun.

54:55.667 --> 54:56.752
Why are you back so soon?

54:57.044 --> 54:58.754
That hurts, Master Sergeant.

54:58.921 --> 55:02.382
I've appeared to resolve the crisis, sir.

55:02.549 --> 55:04.301
Should I prepare the meal right away, sir?

55:04.384 --> 55:05.844
Don't be so dramatic.

55:05.928 --> 55:08.889
Yeah, I missed your shit soup. Let's go.

55:08.972 --> 55:11.225
- Kang Seong-jae, you ready?
- I'm ready, sir.

55:11.308 --> 55:12.476
Let's move out.

55:12.559 --> 55:13.936
Let's go!

55:14.019 --> 55:15.896
- Let's go!
- Yeah!

55:21.819 --> 55:23.237
Now I feel like

55:24.071 --> 55:25.280
I'm in my own skin again.

55:25.531 --> 55:26.532
You know?

55:27.741 --> 55:29.076
- What is it, kid?
- No...

55:31.578 --> 55:33.831
- It's nothing, sir.
- Look at the state of this place

55:33.914 --> 55:35.123
while I was gone.

55:35.332 --> 55:37.668
How am I to discharge peacefully
with things like this?

55:40.504 --> 55:42.923
You must've had a hard time
because of that punk Kwan-cheol.

55:43.257 --> 55:44.716
Don't worry. I'm here now.

55:52.474 --> 55:54.184
- Kang Seong-jae.
- Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

55:56.061 --> 55:57.062
Thanks for the food.

55:57.604 --> 55:58.605
Enjoy your meal, sir.

56:00.232 --> 56:01.650
What's this? What's going on with you two?

56:01.942 --> 56:03.151
Did something happen?

56:04.444 --> 56:07.823
Ah, aren't we colleagues
serving in the army together?

56:09.283 --> 56:12.369
You've gotten soft,
calling your senior a colleague.

56:13.203 --> 56:14.496
Hey, Kim Kwan-cheol.

56:14.830 --> 56:17.040
What did you do to Kang Seong-jae?

56:17.124 --> 56:19.877
What are you talking about?
Do I have to worry about a junior?

56:24.923 --> 56:26.383
You two smiled without me.

56:26.925 --> 56:28.218
You smiled again.

56:30.262 --> 56:31.930
You had it tough with the typhoon.

56:32.014 --> 56:34.057
I'm glad no one got hurt.

56:34.141 --> 56:35.225
How did you get through it?

56:35.517 --> 56:36.602
By demonstrating leadership skills
I learned from you

56:36.685 --> 56:38.353
I, Hwang Seok-ho...

56:38.437 --> 56:40.689
was able to overcome the crisis.

56:41.315 --> 56:42.399
All right.

56:43.150 --> 56:46.194
The Master Sergeant foraged for greens
and mushrooms in the mountains

56:46.278 --> 56:49.448
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae
cooked with the combat rations

56:49.573 --> 56:50.699
so we were able to endure.

56:52.868 --> 56:54.036
What happened?

56:56.872 --> 56:59.708
- Well, sir.
- Everyone could have been in danger!

57:01.209 --> 57:03.837
Aren't there regulations
to prepare for these situations?

57:03.921 --> 57:06.131
What were you thinking,
not knowing the proper regulations!

57:07.132 --> 57:08.342
I'm sorry, sir.

57:35.661 --> 57:36.745
SAVORY SESAME OIL

57:45.754 --> 57:49.132
DISASTER SITUATION ENDED

57:49.967 --> 57:52.219
You have completed

57:52.302 --> 57:53.971
the "Typhoon on a Meal Tray" Quest.

57:54.429 --> 57:55.430
INTERMEDIATE COOK

57:55.514 --> 57:59.142
Changing class to Intermediate Cook.

58:17.077 --> 58:18.495
STAMINA
A NEW PROFICIENCY HAS BEEN ACTIVATED

58:29.339 --> 58:31.550
By changing class to Intermediate Cook

58:32.009 --> 58:34.428
you can now cook five-star dishes.

59:00.704 --> 59:03.123
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

59:03.749 --> 59:05.375
Are you talking about Officers' Mess, sir?

59:05.459 --> 59:06.501
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae

59:06.585 --> 59:08.253
will showcase his cooking.

59:08.336 --> 59:11.048
Complete a five-star dish
for the Regimental Commander.

59:11.131 --> 59:13.842
I don't think a cook from an outpost
can do anything here.

59:13.925 --> 59:16.636
I guess you have to be this good
to be a soldier in the Officers' Mess.

59:18.847 --> 59:20.307
If it's not a five-star dish

59:20.515 --> 59:23.310
- it won't satisfy Regimental Commander.
- Are you going to leave like this?

59:23.643 --> 59:24.895
Sorry I'm late.

59:24.978 --> 59:26.480
Can't you see we've already eaten?

59:26.563 --> 59:29.399
At this rate,
the quest will be a complete failure.
